markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Guiding Students through Coding Levels 

<img src="https://images.code.org/53796bf2dca42a298321692071188a94-image-1777991333557.png" alt="icon of a student with question marks" width="150px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 80px 0px 20px;">

Students sometimes need support when coding with AI. Some common struggles are: 
- Skip reading the existing code
- Don’t understand the context
- Jump straight to asking AI



## Steps for success

This protocol helps students understand, modify, and improve their code.

<div style="width:100%; max-width:760px; margin:20px 0px;">

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🔍 Understand the Starter Code</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Help students make sense of what is already there before trying to change it.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Try a whole-group walkthrough of the starter code, or have students pair up and explain what the code is doing.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">📌 Locate the TODO in the Comments</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Direct students to the TODO sections, which highlight where changes or additions need to be made.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Have students point to the exact place where the new code should go.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🧠 Plan the Behavior in Words</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Before jumping into code, have students describe what they want the program to do in plain language. This builds clarity and intention.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🤖 Prompt the AI</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Support students in writing a clear prompt using structure: Context, Goal, Constraints, and Output Expectations, so the AI can generate useful code.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🔁 Test and Refine</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Encourage students to run their code, check if it works, and make improvements. Students should expect to adjust both their code and their prompts.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

</div>



> #### As you work through these coding levels, practice using these steps yourself. Notice how clear planning and prompting improve the AI’s responses, and think about how you will model and scaffold this process for your students.


 
MARKDOWN
